{%- comment -%}
  AJ Join — the capture page ads point at.

  THE OFFER IS ACCESS, NOT A DISCOUNT. Every instinct says to put "10% off your
  first order" here, and this store cannot afford it: the Yoink is already
  clamped near cost and the Bargain Bin runs at a 20% margin floor, so another
  discount on top comes straight out of a contribution that is $12.67 on a median
  order. Early access costs nothing.

  AND IT PROMISES NO SEND FREQUENCY. An earlier version said "one email a day",
  which committed the business to a cadence nobody had decided on. The list is
  the asset; the schedule is a decision for later, and the copy should not have
  spent it in advance.

  IT ASKS FOR ONE THING. Every extra field costs conversion, and the whole point
  of the page is the email address — the business monetises on repeat visits, so
  the acquisition unit is a returning reader rather than a first order.

  Uses Shopify's own `customer` form, so a submission creates a customer
  subscribed to email marketing and lands in Shopify Email with nothing to
  maintain and nothing to pay for.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign heading = section.settings.heading | default: 'Get first look at the good stuff'
  assign posted = false
  if form.posted_successfully?
    assign posted = true
  endif
-%}

<div
  class="aj-join color-{{ section.settings.color_scheme }} section spacing-style"
  style="{% render 'spacing-style', settings: section.settings %}"
>
  <div class="page-width aj-join__inner">
    <div class="aj-join__copy">
      {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <p class="aj-join__eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      <h1 class="aj-join__heading">{{ heading | escape }}</h1>

      {%- comment -%}
        THE OFFER, NAMED ON THE PAGE THE AD PROMISES IT ON.

        A new setting rather than edited copy, because heading and subheading are
        theme-editor values this file cannot reach — a default only renders while
        the setting is absent from the template JSON, which is exactly the case
        for a setting that did not exist until now.

        THE QUALIFIER IS NOT OPTIONAL. The signup code excludes
        `yoink-of-the-day`, `bargain-bin` and `tee-of-the-week` by tag, so "10%
        off" unqualified is false on the very products this store leads with.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if section.settings.offer != blank -%}
        <p class="aj-join__offer">{{ section.settings.offer | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.subheading != blank -%}
        <p class="aj-join__subheading">{{ section.settings.subheading | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      <ul class="aj-join__points" role="list">
        {%- for i in (1..3) -%}
          {%- assign key = 'point_' | append: i -%}
          {%- assign point = section.settings[key] -%}
          {%- if point != blank -%}
            <li class="aj-join__point">{{ point | escape }}</li>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>

    </div>

    <div class="aj-join__form-col">
      {%- comment -%}
        THE CROW PERCHES ON THE CARD, which is why it sits in this column rather
        than under the copy. Its feet want to land on the card's top edge, so it
        is a sibling with a negative bottom margin rather than a background — a
        background would crop on narrow screens and there would be no way to keep
        the feet on the edge as the card grows.

        `aria-hidden` and an empty alt: it is decoration. A screen reader
        announcing "crow holding a diamond" before the email field would be
        noise in front of the one thing this page asks for.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if section.settings.art != blank -%}
        <img
          class="aj-join__art"
          src="{{ section.settings.art | image_url: width: 520 }}"
          alt=""
          aria-hidden="true"
          width="260"
          height="260"
          loading="lazy"
        >
      {%- endif -%}

    <div class="aj-join__form-card">
      {%- if posted -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          The confirmation has to do a job, not just say thanks: someone who has
          just handed over an email is the most likely they will ever be to look
          at today's deal, and the homepage is one tap away.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <p class="aj-join__success">{{ section.settings.success_text | escape }}</p>
        <a class="aj-join__cta" href="{{ routes.root_url }}">See today's Yoink</a>
      {%- else -%}
        {%- form 'customer', class: 'aj-join__form' -%}
          <input type="hidden" name="contact[tags]" value="{{ section.settings.tag | escape }}">

          {%- if form.errors -%}
            <p class="aj-join__error">
              {{ form.errors.translated_fields.email | capitalize }}
              {{ form.errors.messages.email }}
            </p>
          {%- endif -%}

          <label class="visually-hidden" for="aj-join-email">Email address</label>
          <input
            id="aj-join-email"
            class="aj-join__input"
            type="email"
            name="contact[email]"
            placeholder="you@example.com"
            autocomplete="email"
            required
          >

          <button class="aj-join__submit" type="submit">
            {{ section.settings.button_text | escape }}
          </button>

          {%- if section.settings.fine_print != blank -%}
            <p class="aj-join__fine">{{ section.settings.fine_print | escape }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endform -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  .aj-join__inner {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--padding-lg, 2rem);
    align-items: center;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .aj-join__inner { grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 0.9fr; gap: var(--padding-xl, 3rem); }
  }

  .aj-join__heading { margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
  .aj-join__subheading { margin: 0 0 1.25rem; opacity: 0.8; font-size: 1.05rem; }

  .aj-join__points { margin: 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; display: grid; gap: 0.5rem; }

  /* A drawn tick rather than a bullet: the list is three promises, and it should
     read as reassurance rather than as a table of contents. */
  .aj-join__point {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.6rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .aj-join__point::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0.15rem;
    top: 0.45em;
    width: 0.55rem;
    height: 0.3rem;
    border-left: 2px solid currentColor;
    border-bottom: 2px solid currentColor;
    transform: rotate(-45deg);
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  .aj-join__form-card {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: var(--padding-lg, 2rem);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: rgb(var(--color-foreground-rgb) / 0.04);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgb(var(--color-foreground-rgb) / 0.1);
  }

  .aj-join__form { display: grid; gap: 0.75rem; }

  .aj-join__input {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    width: 100%;
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    border: 1px solid rgb(var(--color-foreground-rgb) / 0.25);
    background: rgb(var(--color-background-rgb, 255 255 255));
    color: inherit;
  }

  .aj-join__submit {
    padding: 0.95rem 1rem;
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: 8px;
    cursor: pointer;
    background: rgb(var(--color-foreground-rgb));
    color: rgb(var(--color-background-rgb, 255 255 255));
  }

  .aj-join__submit:hover { opacity: 0.9; }

  .aj-join__fine { margin: 0; font-size: 0.8125rem; opacity: 0.65; }
  .aj-join__error { margin: 0; font-size: 0.875rem; color: #b3261e; }
  .aj-join__success { margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 600; }

  .aj-join__cta {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
    background: rgb(var(--color-foreground-rgb));
    color: rgb(var(--color-background-rgb, 255 255 255));
  }

  /*
    ON BRAND, 7 AUG 2026. This page was the only surface on the store that could
    have come from any Shopify theme — a white sheet, a black button, a system
    heading — while every other surface is teal, yellow or purple. It is also the
    page paid traffic points at, so it was the worst one to leave generic.

    THE PURPLE IS THE FOOTER'S PURPLE and the yellow is the price badge's yellow;
    nothing new is invented here. The heading takes Flashy at real scale for the
    reason aj-brand.css already documents — a display face needs room or it reads
    thin — and the eyebrow takes Ohpixel, which is the face this brand uses for
    short uppercase labels and the one that carries the 8-bit feel.
  */
  /*
    THE COLOUR GOES ON A CLASS THIS FILE OWNS, not on the section.

    The first attempt set it on `.aj-join` and shipped an UNREADABLE page: the
    background computed to `transparent` — the theme wins that property on the
    section element — while `color: #fff` applied fine, so every line of copy was
    white on white. Only the yellow eyebrow and ticks survived.

    Measured on the live page: `class="aj-join color- section"` — the colour
    scheme setting is EMPTY, so the theme's own scheme classes are malformed here
    and there is nothing to coordinate with. `.aj-join__inner` is defined in this
    file and targeted by nothing else, which makes it the one element whose
    background cannot be taken away.

    Background and text colour now live on the SAME element. They can no longer
    be separated, which is the actual bug — not the shade.
  */
  .aj-join__inner {
    background-color: #7a3fa0;
    color: #ffffff;
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  .aj-join__eyebrow {
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
  }

  .aj-join__inner .aj-join__heading {
    font-family: "Flashy", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
    line-height: 1.02;
    color: #fff;
  }

  .aj-join__inner .aj-join__subheading { color: #ffffff; opacity: 0.92; }
  .aj-join__inner .aj-join__point { color: #ffffff; }
  .aj-join__inner .aj-join__point::before { opacity: 1; color: var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000); }

  /* The card stays light: a form is the one thing here that should look like a
     form, and white on purple is the strongest contrast the palette offers. */
  .aj-join__inner .aj-join__form-card {
    background: #fff;
    color: var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828);
    border: 0;
    border-top: 4px solid var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
    border-radius: 14px;
  }

  .aj-join__inner .aj-join__submit,
  .aj-join__inner .aj-join__cta {
    background: var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
    color: var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828);
    border: 0;
    font-weight: 800;
  }
  .aj-join__inner .aj-join__submit:hover,
  .aj-join__inner .aj-join__cta:hover { filter: brightness(1.08); }

  /*
    THE CROW, AS A SETTING RATHER THAN A HARDCODED ASSET. The pixel art lives in
    Shopify Files, not in the theme, and a theme asset url carries a version hash
    that changes on every deploy. A picker also means the art can be swapped
    seasonally without a code change.

    `image-rendering: pixelated` is the whole point: without it the browser
    smooths 8-bit art on a high-DPI screen and it stops reading as pixel art.
  */
  /* The offer is the reason someone clicked, so it sits above the fold and
     takes the yellow — the same badge colour the storefront uses for a saving. */
  .aj-join__inner .aj-join__offer {
    display: inline-block;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    padding: 0.55rem 1rem;
    background: var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
    color: var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828);
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  /*
    PERCHED, NOT PLACED. The negative bottom margin is what puts the crow's feet
    on the card's top edge instead of leaving it hovering above a gap. It is
    tuned to the art's own transparent footer, so a different image will need a
    different number — which is the cost of a perch and worth it.

    `image-rendering: pixelated` is load-bearing: without it a browser smooths
    8-bit art on a high-DPI screen and it stops reading as pixel art.
  */
  .aj-join__form-col { position: relative; }

  .aj-join__art {
    display: block;
    width: 150px;
    height: auto;
    margin: 0 0 -14px auto;
    margin-right: 2rem;
    image-rendering: pixelated;
    /* Above the card, so the overlap reads as standing on it. */
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .aj-join__art { width: 190px; margin-bottom: -18px; }
  }

{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "AJ Join",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "default": "One a day, gone in 24 hours",
      "info": "Small pixel-face line above the heading. Uppercased automatically."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "offer",
      "label": "Offer line",
      "default": "Take 10% off your first order — full-price items, one use.",
      "info": "Must match what any ad pointing here promises. Leave blank to hide."
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "art",
      "label": "Pixel art",
      "info": "The crow. Lives in Files rather than the theme so it can be swapped without a deploy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The capture page for ads and link-in-bio. Submissions create a customer subscribed to email marketing, which Shopify Email sends to."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Get first look at the good stuff" },
    {
      "type": "text", "id": "subheading", "label": "Subheading",
      "default": "A new deal every morning and a Bargain Bin that rotates weekly. Join the list and we'll show you how it works."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "point_1", "label": "Point 1", "default": "A new deal every morning, deeply discounted" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "point_2", "label": "Point 2", "default": "The Bargain Bin, refreshed weekly — always at least 25% off" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "point_3", "label": "Point 3", "default": "We email when it's worth it, not on a timer" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "button_text", "label": "Button", "default": "Count me in" },
    {
      "type": "text", "id": "fine_print", "label": "Fine print",
      "default": "No spam. Unsubscribe in one click, whenever."
    },
    {
      "type": "text", "id": "success_text", "label": "Success message",
      "default": "You're in. Check your inbox — we'll explain how this works."
    },
    {
      "type": "text", "id": "tag", "label": "Customer tag", "default": "join-page",
      "info": "Tags the customer so this page's signups can be told apart from footer signups."
    },
    { "type": "color_scheme", "id": "color_scheme", "label": "Color scheme", "default": "scheme-1" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Padding" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding-block-start", "label": "Top", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 60 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding-block-end", "label": "Bottom", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 60 }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "AJ Join" }]
}
{% endschema %}